/api.github.com/users/btmills/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"event":"labeled","commit_id":null,"commit_url":null,"created_at":"2015-04-03T21:04:40Z","label":{"name":"rule","color":"fbca04"},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/89421739","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/2229#issuecomment-89421739","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2229","id":89421739,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg5NDIxNzM5","user":{"login":"btmills","id":1709537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDk1Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1709537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills","html_url":"https://github.com/btmills","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-03T21:12:36Z","updated_at":"2015-04-03T21:12:36Z","body":"The current implementation uses a regex to look for newlines in the raw source code. Using tokens simplifies the logic greatly.\n\nMore specific to this issue, in my opinion, comments should be allowed at the end of the line by default, no option necessary. Thoughts?\n\nAlso, while I'm at it, the current error message is `Newline is {always/never} expected after a \"var\" statement.` Would it be a breaking change if the messages were altered? At the very least \"var\" should be \"let\" or \"const\" where appropriate, but I'd rather just change to \"...after variable declarations.\" Further, this isn't just checking for a newline, but for a blank line. The naming seems misleading to me. So, pie in the sky proposal: deprecate `newline-after-var`, add a new rule, name TBD (`blank-line-after-variable-declaration` is way too long), same always/never option, whose messages are `Unexpected blank line after variable declarations.` and `Expected blank line after variable declarations.`\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/89421739/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"btmills","id":1709537,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MDk1Mzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1709537?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills","html_url":"https://github.com/btmills","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btmills/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/89423882","html_url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/2229#issuecomment-89423882","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/2229","id":89423882,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDg5NDIzODgy","user":{"login":"cvisco","id":1328232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjgyMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1328232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco","html_url":"https://github.com/cvisco","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-04-03T21:23:10Z","updated_at":"2015-04-03T21:23:10Z","body":"@btmills: 100% Agree permitting trailing comments _should_ be default. I was thinking at first someone might not want that, but I just realized there is a separate rule for dealing with trailing comments anyway: `no-inline-comments`.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/comments/89423882/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cvisco","id":1328232,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjgyMzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1328232?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cvisco","html_url":"https://github.com/cvisco","followers_url":